---
description: Respond to the caretaker’s goal using the actual owned scene, scope and authorized local artifacts.
args:
  goal: string
returns: GrimoireSceneOutcome
---
Determine whether the caretaker wants an explanation, preservation of the current scene, a private scene draft or a note. Compose scene reading, interpretation, currentness and exact staging capabilities according to the observed goal and real feedback. A proposal or permission is not proof that a requested scene or note was staged.

Keep the installed current scene, actual caretaker scope and any proposed destination distinct. Use only real observed anchors and usable authored assets; do not invent artwork or transfer another owner’s scene. If the native frontier moves or authority is missing, interpret the actual result before choosing the next useful computation. Retain a requested local artifact only on its valid native basis and return its actual reference or the supported requested finding. This computation does not publish or mutate the owned world outside those exact native boundaries.
